    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 the full suite (17 tests across Cp01\u2013Cp09) is green and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (mapped to column `customer_code`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, assign the code before saving via a new `assignCustomerCode(lastName)` helper:\n   - `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (`java.util.Locale.ROOT`, guarded for short names).\n   - `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits via `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`. Computed before the save, so it equals one more than the current owner count.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it into the GET response.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table (the tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL column is required; updated all four for consistency).\n\nThe Cp09 test confirms both the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefix formatting and the global monotonic sequence (each new owner's number is exactly one greater than the previous).",
